BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206163@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261009T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: CTE's Lasting Impact on the NFL 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 13 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 06163\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nWhat does the latest scie
 nce reveal about the lasting impact of contact sports on the brain - and h
 ow can that knowledge help protect the next generation of athletes? Join u
 s for a timely ’Quin Chat with Chris Nowinski\, PhD\, and Daniel Daneshv
 ar\, MD\, PhD\, lead authors of a landmark study recently published in the
  British Medical Journal. Examining former NFL players who died between 20
 16 and 2021\, the research proved that at least one in four had the brain 
 disease chronic traumatic encephalopathy (CTE) - a finding that made globa
 l headlines and raises urgent questions about the future of football and o
 ther contact sports. Together\, Dr. Nowinski and Dr. Daneshvar will unpack
  the study’s most consequential findings\, evolving questions\, and what
  science is revealing about the neurological effects of repeated head impa
 cts.\n\nA former Harvard football player and WWE wrestler whose career was
  cut short by concussions\, Dr. Nowinski is the co-founder of the Concussi
 on & CTE Foundation and the Boston University CTE Center Brain Bank. Dr. D
 aneshvar is Chair of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at Mass General 
 Brigham and Harvard Medical School\, Chief of Brain Injury Rehabilitation 
 at Spaulding Rehabilitation\, and Director of the HealthSpan Lab. The even
 ing will be moderated by Nell Scovell\, a former Boston Globe sports journ
 alist\, “Lean In” co-author\, and TV writer (“The Simpsons\,” “C
 oach\,” creator\, “Sabrina the Teenage Witch.”) and the discussion w
 ill offer a candid look at what the science tells us now—and where playe
 rs\, families\, and the sports community go from here.\n\n*This event is c
 omplimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and 
 refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made 
 at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206163
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
