SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Modern Parenting - Navigating Teen Mental Health Togeth
 er
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 62 spot
 s left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/eve
 nts/206905\n\n7:00PM Reception\, 7:30PM Discussion\n\nWhat is simply part 
 of being a teenager—and when does it warrant a closer look? Join us for 
 an expert-led ’Quin Chat exploring the mental health and well-being of t
 oday’s teenagers and how parents can better understand and support them 
 through these formative years. At a time marked by significant physical\, 
 emotional\, and social change - and amplified by social media\, constant c
 onnectivity\, academic pressures\, and an increasingly digital world - our
  panel will explore what constitutes typical teenage behavior\, signs that
  may warrant greater attention\, and how parents can approach difficult co
 nversations and offer meaningful support.\n\nModerated by Kimberlyn Leary\
 , PhD\, MPA\, associate professor of psychology at the Harvard Medical Sch
 ool and Senior Advisor at McLean Hospital\, the conversation will bring to
 gether adolescent mental health and pediatric experts Cecil Webster\, MD\,
  psychiatrist\, psychoanalyst\, and CEO of Webster Clinic\; Jacqueline Buc
 hanan\, MD\, psychiatrist at Webster Clinic\; and Essential Pediatrics Co-
 Founders Brenda Anders Pring\, MD\, and Christina Nordt\, MD. Together\, t
 hey will offer expert perspective on changing moods\, growing independence
 \, anxiety\, social pressures\, technology\, and the evolving parent-teen 
 relationship—with practical guidance for helping teenagers navigate it a
 ll.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complim
 entary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all
  cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206905
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206907@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: From Head Of The Charles to Los Angeles 2028 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: Sports & Games\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 101 spots 
 left\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/206907\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\n\nAs the rowing
  world turns its attention to Boston for one of the sport’s most celebra
 ted weekends\, join us for a timely ’Quin Chat with NBC10 Boston Host Ha
 nnah Donnelly and two-time Olympic rower and Massachusetts native\, Kristi
  Wagner. Fresh off competing at the World Rowing Championships\, Wagner wi
 ll share an inside look at her experience on the international stage\, the
  training and determination required to compete among the world’s best\,
  and what comes next as she sets her sights on earning another Olympic ber
 th for the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Donnelly and Wagn
 er will dive into the excitement surrounding this year’s Head Of The Cha
 rles Regatta\, where Wagner will once again take to the water\, and explor
 e what makes the iconic race such a defining moment for Boston and the glo
 bal rowing community. Their conversation will also take a broader look at 
 the state of U.S. women’s rowing\, the athletes and momentum shaping its
  future\, and the road ahead as the sport builds toward Los Angeles in 202
 8. From racing on the Charles to competing on the world’s biggest stage\
 , the evening offers a rare glimpse into the life of an elite athlete and 
 the ambition\, preparation\, and perseverance behind the pursuit of Olympi
 c excellence.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly as
 k that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of t
 he event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206907
CATEGORIES:Sports & Games
END:VEVENT
